<title>ITALY: Italy's Venice sees May CPI at 0.5 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Venice sees May CPI at 0.5 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>VENICE, Italy 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Venice said its May consumer price index stood at 0.5 percent month-on-month and 1.3 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In April, the Venice inflation rate fell 0.1 and rose 1.5 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Venice was one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Tuesday and Wednesday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.89 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to April 1997):</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		   0.5    (-0.1)	1.3    (1.5)</p>
<p>    Food				0.0    (-0.5)     -2.3   (-1.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.1     (0.0)	2.8    (3.0)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges 0.4     (0.5)	4.5    (3.7)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 1.3    (-0.1)	2.1    (1.7)</p>
<p>    Health services		 0.5     (0.0)	2.0    (1.8)</p>
<p>    Transportation		  0.3    (-0.1)	2.1    (2.2)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture  -0.1    (-0.1)     -2.6   (-2.5)</p>
<p>    Education			 0.1    (-0.1)	4.5    (4.7)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	0.4     (0.1)	3.9    (5.4)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services     1.3    (-0.1)	1.2    (0.5)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
